sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-02> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-02--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-02--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch15-02: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.71" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.711"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.73"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The comparative rule, that the most tapered eggs are large relative to the parent, can be fit directly to open shape and adult-size data spanning most bird orders. Those same datasets have already been used to compare anatomical and incubation correlates, so the pattern is resolvable and the pressure mechanism is only proxied. A positive size–asymmetry slope would support the rule Thompson states and would still leave rival causes of taper in play." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Regress egg asymmetry on egg size relative to adult body size across species, with a phylogenetic control, and inspect named cases such as guillemots, sandpipers, terns, and Apteryx. The common rule is supported by a positive relationship and by the stated exceptions having large oviducts; the pressure explanation is not tested unless oviduct pressure, rather than relative size alone, is measured." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Relative size is a proxy for the pressure Thompson invokes, and flight or nesting correlates can produce the same pattern.", "Oviduct dimensions in the open file are not pressure records along the forming egg." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-02--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch15-02--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-02--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch15-02 by Grok 4.7: 0.74" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.74"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch15-02--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
